In comp.sys.dec Bernhard Strathewerd <mendite@altmuehlnet.de> wrote:
> Hello!

> I wanna set up truecolor on our Alphas for better use of gimp. I found
> nothing in the handbooks of Dec-Unix, in X Administrator Guid and in the
> manpages which says me which file
> or program i have to edit/execute for the change of colordeep. I=B4m be
> happy about a tip!

Have you looked at the man page for the X server? Dunno if OPEN3D is
necessary to get TrueColor support (you should have a license for this
is you have a 24-bit video card though).

I've gotten 24-bit to work but that was at an old client site. The man
page for the X server should help you out. There is a confuration file
you need to edit which contains startup options to the X server where
you tell it to go 24-bit. Nevertheless, what does the output of
'xdpyinfo' show? Even though your default visual is 8-bit, the X
server should be smart enough to show that you're 24-bit capable. Your
software, gimp in this case, should be smart enough to use this visual
when displaying, even though your default is 8-bit.

> Bernhard Strathewerd

