David A Froble <davef@tsoft-inc.com> writes...
}But, if it is just presentation, just why is it VMS that gets
}the "as long as it is profitable" tag?
} 
}Dave

Are you sure that it did?

There seems to me to be 3 ways to interpret the statement:

"We will A, and we will B, and we will C as long as it is profitable"
can be either

  (A) and (B) and (C as long as it is profitable)

or it can be

  (A) and ((B and C) as long as it is profitable)

  (this goes with the division between "support" and "promote")

or it can be

  (A and B and C) as long as it is profitable

It's impossible to say which was meant without hearing it, and even
those who heard it probably can't really be certain which was meant. 

I suspect that the "we will keep doing things that are profitable and
stop doing things that are not profitable" is the best interpretation
of what was meant.

--- Carl



