Michael Dalwood <Michael.Dalwood@health.sa.gov.au> wrote in message
news:7nit5b$kbd@internal.sa.gov.au...
> Hi,
>
> I am trying to configure a DECHub 900 Multiswitch, with a few DECrepeater
> 900TM attached.

If you have only 900TM modules, there isn't a lot to configure. Each of them
consists of a single LAN segment with 32 ports on it. You could connect
different 900TM modules to different LAN's, but you would need a switch
module (900EE, for instance) to interconnect those LAN's.

>
> I have been using HUBwatch without any real success.

Which version of HUBwatch? The oldest one that I know is V3.x for VMS. That
one should be able to configure your modules.

>
> Does anyone know of a product that can remotely configure these DEC
> products?

Theoretically,  any SNMP manager could manage those critters. But if you you
are not familiar with the Simple Network Management Protocol it is
definitely not Simple!

>
> I have configured the Multiswitch with a In-Band IP address.

That should be a good start, both for HUBwatch or any other SNMP manager.
The backplane itself has no management agent; it needs an agent from one of
the installed modules. You could try to configure one of the 900TM's with
it's own IP address, and then direct HUBwatch to that address. You will be
able to see only that module, but at least you can verify if HUBwatch is
working at all.

Hope this helps a little!

Regards,

Bart Zorn







