In article <7nit5b$kbd@internal.sa.gov.au>, "Michael Dalwood" <Michael.Dalwood@health.sa.gov.au> writes:
>I am trying to configure a DECHub 900 Multiswitch, with a few DECrepeater
>900TM attached.

Nice Boxes.

But PORTswitch 900 TP/12 is now the way to go (instead of the
DECrepeater 900TM).

And what do you want to get ? One shared (!) Ethernet Segment with
"few" times 32 attached nodes ?
In all other cases, you got the wrong or to few components.

>I have been using HUBwatch without any real success.

HUBwatch ? Where ? On OpenVMS or on ULTRIX/dUNIX or on Win32 ?
HUBwatch is the old name of the ClearVISN MultiChassis Manager
and is for years now only available on Win32 (current is V6.3).
Last version on VMS was V3.1 (way before it was renamed to CVISN MCM),

Real Success ? What is the problem ? What is the error message ?
Do you get connection ?

>Does anyone know of a product that can remotely configure these DEC
>products?

You got the right product.
Maybe you haven't got the current version but it doesn't matter in your case.
HUBWatch V3.1 does not have any problems managing such old modules like
the DECrepeater 900TM).

You may be able to configure the hub with a generic SNMP manager
(DECmcc, SPECTRUM, OpenView, NetView, NetManager, ...) and the
right MIBs (see http:://www.networks.digital.com/dr/hubs/mibs)
compiled/enrolled in the manager, too. 
But then again, it is still not easy at all.
You've got to know SNMP and MIBs in detail...

>I have configured the Multiswitch with a In-Band IP address.

Did you configure the SNMP config, too ?
Did you connect the management system (HUBwatch) on the module in the slot
which you selected for the In-Band Adress ?
Did you specify the SNMP community configuration in the HUBwatch config, too ?
If you are running Hubwatch V3.1 on VMS, did you start Hubwatch ?
	($ @SYS$STARTUP:HUBWATCH$STARTUP)

