>microvax 3100 connect to a microvax 4000 via telephone line using
>decnet, I was able to use speed 4800, 9600 but not 19.2k, tried to login
>to microvax4000 via telephone line at 19.2k but no luck when running
>decnet. any suggestion????
>
LTA lines are totally unsupported for DDCMP.  The LAT protocol timing
parameters are not compatible with DDCMP.  It might work under some
conditions.

IMHO: If a VAX or VAXstation identifies a port as being a TTcn: such as
TTA0: or CSA0: or OPA0:, do not use it for this purpose.  TTcn: class
devices have effectively no buffering and will easily saturate your system
when used for communication links.
Limit them to interactive use, or restrict the baud rate to about 1200 baud.

I have seen 1200 baud on TTA2: on a VAXstation 2000 bugcheck VMS 4.7.  That
is about a .9 VUP machine, so obviously faster machines can handle a faster
speed.  YMMV.

Using serial links for reliable networking would involve getting the
terminal options that support DMA and MODEM control.

An alternative is to obtain a box that can translate ethernet to a dial-up
line.  Several Vendors sell them, or you can roll your own using a LINUX
box.

-John





