  Maybe yes, maybe no...

  That depends on which graphics controller is in use in the DEC 3000 model
  300 -- there was an integrated (HX) controller, and there were various
  other controllers sold with the system.  

  There are resolutions shared between the VRT19-HA and VRC16-HA monitors, 
  such as the rather commonly-used setting of 1280 by 1024 at 72 Hz.  (This
  is the "maybe yes" part.)  There are also resolutions that are not shared,
  with the VRC16-HA having more combinations.  (You guessed it, this is the
  "maybe no" part...)

