Dave Greenwood wrote:
> 
> I just received a PW500AU workstation, but it doesn't have a graphics
> card.  Until the card arrives I was hoping to use a vt220 (lookalike)
> as a console.  I tried hooking it up to both COM ports and tried a
> couple of different baud rates, but so far nothing has shown up on
> the screen.
> 
> Assuming I can use a vt220 as a console on that workstation, can (will)
> someone tell me the settings I need to use?
> 
> TIA,
> Dave
> --------------
> Dave Greenwood                Internet: Greenwoodde@ORNL.GOV
> Oak Ridge National Lab        %STD-W-DISCLAIMER, I only speak for myself

Just some basics, and maybe you know all this already.  I do not have
a PW500AU so the info is generic.  I use terminals as the console for
various Alphas.  The port labeled COM1 is the port to use.  It is
usually a 9-pin (DB9) port.  The pins are as follows:

1 - data carrier detect
2 - receive data
3 - transmit data
4 - data terminal ready
5 - ground
6 - data set ready
7 - request to send
8 - clear to send
9 - ring indicator

You can get by with just pins 2,3, and 5.  The cable must be a null modem,
ie; ground to ground, transmit to receive, receive to transmit.  Speed for
the console is ususlly 9600 baud.

Dave

