Max wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> I am trying to install the OpenVMS hobbiest CD version of 7.2.
> 
> Here's what I got:
> 
> 1) Vaxstation 4000VLC with 8 megs
> 2) RZ24L Hard drive
> 3) 2X SCSI CDROM, Model#CR-503-B (Matsushita-Kotobuki) labeled
> Compaq device type listed as Compaq CD-ROM CR-...
> 
> Here's what happens:
> 
> a) I can boot from the CD-ROM (DKA400:) with no problem
> b) I can't do the backup up to the RZ24L, I get an error
> "SABKUP$DKA400: offline. Mount verification in progress"
> 
> At this point it locks up.
> 
> I do have 5.5 on the RZ24 drive if that helps.
> 
> Should parity be set on the CDROM or Term Power?

Parity should always be enabled on any SCSI devices connected to a VAX.

Termination should only be set on the devices at the physical end of the
SCSI bus.  The VLC is at one end and is terminated.  There should also
be a terminator either at the external SCSI connector or at the end of
the external SCSI chain.

No devices should be supplying termination power.

I wouldn't be suprised to find out that VMS 7.2 just doesn't like your
CD-ROM and that you need to get another one.

Good luck!

