Howard,

Assuming that you are going to attach the 8.4GB drive to the same IDE
cable as the 2.1GB drive, set the jumpers on the 2.1GB drive to the
"master" setting, and set the 8.4GB to "slave".

If you are running Win 95 SR2 or later or Win 98, it is MUCH better to
partition the 8.4GB drive as one large partition, format the 8.4GB as
bootable, then copy everything from the 2.1GB to the 8.4GB drive.
Then reverse master and slave jumper settings.

Windows 95/98 likes it much better if the C: drive is the larger drive
because it tries to install everything on the C: drive, and even if
you tell it otherwise, a software install will add a lot of rubbish to
the C: drive... Ben Myers

