First of all, you probably didn't loose any of you data.  The console is
in flash in the AS200 and doesn't have anything directly to do with the
contents of you disk.

What needs to be done depends a bit on your AS200.  There were two
variants that affect the console: half flash (512KB) and full flash
(1MB).

If you have a full flash model, your machine has both SRM and ARC
consoles.  Enter the command "SET OS NT" at the >>> prompt and then
cycle power.  If the machine comes back up in ARC, you are done.  There
is a corresponding command in the ARC console to switch to the VMS
console.  This may have been executed unintentionally.


If you have half flash, you will need to reload the ARC console from a
firmware CDROM or an appropriate floppy.  If you have half flash, there
is no way for the machine to "reset itself" to the SRM, since the SRM
isn't even loaded into the machine.  This change can only happen
intentionally.

Good luck!

