I am not arguing, that VMS should not be priced competitively. A box
with VMS will always be more expensive than the same box with Linux.
Probably the box with NT will also always be cheaper, because Windows
sells in astronomical quantities. But VMS should never be more
expensive than Tru64. And it is (on the small boxes). So I hope that
someone at Compaq do think about this. That said, then I think it is
relative optimistic think a 18.4% price decrease will create a
200% increase in quantities sold.

