Roger Woodward wrote:

> does anyone have an idea what the basic cause of the following linker
> error is?
>
> Object file format error in: ...libxyz.a (abc.o)
> local_is_complete: iaux(316)>iauxMax(132) for obj
> libxyz.a(abc.o)
>
> im trying to link a library built with gnu c++ with objects/libraries
> built with dec cc.
>
> libraries built under 3.2.c.  dec cc running under 4.0d

This was a bug in an old GCC version that would corrupt things - we
added an error check in
the linker at some point (V4.0?) so that the bad objects wouldn't
continue to proliferate.
You might be able to "workaround" the error by not using -g on the
compile or link line.

The problem here is that the old objects were built with buggy tools and
the
old linker never complained about the bug (it just did something wrong
silently), and we've since enhanced the linker to complain upfront
rather
than do something incorrect.

At any rate, recompilation with a newer version of the tools is the
recommended fix.

Joe Mario
Compaq Tru64 Development Environment





