Erik Lindberg (lindberg@roguewave.com) wrote:
: Im looking for ways to find various DEC sys info such as physical memory
: size, number of processors, etc, hopefully in the form of one or more
: clever unix commands (like hinv for SGI) or utility scripts.  Got any
: ideas?

Since you mentioned "unix", I'll assume that you're asking in the context of
Digital Unix or Tru64 Unix.

When Digital/Tru64 Unix boots, it displays a hardware inventory of everything
that the kernel is built for and what it actually saw.  The memory size,
number (and speed) of processors are all there.  Use this command to view the
inventory from the error log:

        # uerf -Rr 300 | more
        
