Greg Lindahl wrote:

> mccalpin@frakir.engr.sgi.com (John McCalpin) writes:

> > With this change, this code scales extremely well, delivering
> > something along the lines of a >200x speedup on a 256p system.

> Can you give a citation for this? The only MM5 results I've seen show
> the version which takes a message passing approach giving the best
> performance on an SGI. (The code has been parallelized using a variety
> of methods.) In addition, the current local physics apparently has
> some siginificant load-balancing problems which prevent it from
> reaching that kind of speed-up on any system.

Indeed - if the model uses the "all physics parametrisation in one
column" assumption (which is quite valid down to resolutions of 5 km),
every column of the atmosphere can be computed in parallel.

However, depending on the phenomena in that column (convection takes
place, or not, sun above the horizon or not) the amount of computation
can differ.

This causes load inbalances.

