to this group.

The general opinion when the origional thread covering this was
aired was that OpenVMS was more secure than UNIX based
on anecdotal evidence and the fact that there are more UNIX
CERT advisories than OpenVMS ones. This of course ignored
the fact that Digital did not report at all for vunerabilities which
they later patched for. You seem to be suggesting that in this
instance the OpenVMS fans attitude was and is foolish and I
can only agree with you.

