Patrick Michel wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> Can anyone tell me how to change the standard resolution
> in CDE (i think it is 800x600) ? I have an 17" Monitor and
> like to use 1024 x 768.
> 
> thanks for help

This is not a CDE question, this an X question.
So it depends on what X server you're using. I'm guessing
that you're running Tru64/DU/OSF1, so your X server is
Xdec, and its configuration file is (by default) in
/usr/var/X11/Xserver.conf. 

There's a line in mine that looks like this:
-screen0 1600x1200 -depth 16 -vsync 75 -pn -nice -2

I'd try changing those resolution parameters.
See 'man Xdec' for more details.

hope this helps,
usman



