Paul Bourke wrote:
> 
> How does one getting the machine load? I'm about to do some parallel
> animations on a Dec farm (UNIX) and would like to check the load from
> my C source and not use that machine if the load is too high. Sure
> I can system("uptime") and parse the result....yuk. Surely there's
> a cleaner "standard" way?

As I understand it, things about process information are more or
less guaranteed to be *different* between different operating systems,
which is why there is no POSIXish way to get at process information
at the lower level. I'm no fan of system() in C programs either, but
I'd guess in this case, uptime is the best way to go.

But if anyone knows differently, please, let's hear it.
-usman



