I'd like to clear up an apparent misperception that seems to have taken
root here.

Part of the reasoning behind was not because OpenVMS SMP had a
problem with more than 6-8 CPU's, but more because it was observed that most
commercial workloads implemented on VMS did not take advantage of
more than 6-8 CPU's.  Now, you could say that this was because SMP didn't
scale,
or, because someone didn't write many commercial apps that were decomposed
enough to use more than say, 4 CPUs.

I prefer the latter choice, since many folks implemented their apps on VMS
because
it was easier or simpler than the other choices they had.

My opinions only, not speaking for DEQ or Compaq

