Ben,
  I have a vendor built computer with the AMD K6-2 333 on a 66Mhz bus
board by Amptron (PCChip mfg).  With the multiplier set to 5.5 it does
indeed run at 334 Mhz.  However the throughput on this board is lousy,
with the CPU becoming process bound for too easily.  Plus I needed to up
my RAM to 128MB to keep the system from randomly (but often) locking up
with the processor pegged at 100%.  In my research I notice that AMD
does not recommend the 95Mhz K6-2 333 to be used on any 66Mhz boards.

  Be aware that there was one run of 333's that were spec'ed by AMD to
run on 66 Mhz, they can be identified by the chip marking for processor
type ending in either -ATR-66 or - 66.  If you have one of those go
ahead.

  I plan on buying a motherboard that supports the 95Mhz speed and I
will bet that my performance will be much better.

Good Luck with yours.



Ben Myers wrote:
> 
> Has anybody tried to run the AMD 333Mhz K6-2 with a 66MHz bus clock
> frequency and a clock multiplier of 5.0x ???   The AMD K6-2 spec shows
> BF2-BF1-BF0 pin values up to 5.5x, and I have a 66MHz-only DEC
> computer with all the other things right, i.e. BIOS compatibility and
> voltage regulator to set Vcore to 2.2v.  The AMD spec describes the
> 333 as running at 95Mhz with a 3.5x multiplier, but I figure it should
> not matter how the clock frequency is reached as long as it is not
> overclocked.  (Nope, I'm not a fan of overclocking.  Sorry.)
> 
> Also, what about the 366MHz K6-2 with a 66MHz bus clock frequency and
> a clock multiplier of 5.5x ???
> 
> System is a DEC Celebris FX-2 (or a Venturis FX-2?)
> 
> Thanks much... Ben Myers

