processors than are currently available.  The OpenVMS   Galaxy work targets
limitations that can and do result from SMP scaling,   something that doesn't
become a performance factor until the contention   that arises from reaching
some application-specific number of processors.   (Visit one of the newsgroup
search engines and look for the discussion --   involving Professor Minsky and
a conjecture of his -- that transpired a   while back over in comp.os.vms...)
                     
