My problem is not with those who know little about the industry.  My problem
is with the people in the industry, the computer manufacturers.  HP tried to
base it's future on IA-64.  Now it's scrambling because Intel didn't deliver.
Why wouldn't someone like HP take a look at Alpha?  It's not really a DEC
only CPU now.  It isn't good for their Win9* platforms, but neither is IA-64.

For that matter, why isn't Intel looking at Alpha.  With the capability of
loading PAL code to alter the 'appearance' of the CPU, it might be possible
to have an Alpha chip run software written for the Intel 32-bit chips.  I'm
a bit fuzzy about this, but I seem to remember some discussion of it when the
Alpha was first introduced.

