> took to make Digital an attractive takeover target, which is apparently what
> BPs game plan had been since he took charge.

No argument there.

BP was a giveaway artist.  He gave VMS technology to MS.  A business doesn't
GIVE anything without a good business reason (such as free software licenses
to education institutions, that he should have done) and some plan for it
returning some type of benefits in the future.  Wonder if he's as free with
the ill gotten millions he received for dismantelling DEC?  Hey BP, can I
have some?  I still feel DEC could have made life very miserable for Intel,
or gotten a lot more from them.  The settlement sure seemed to happen pretty
fast.  Guess Intel had enough business sense to grab a gift.

