The deeper issue here, I think, is not that "Japan is better than the US"
or such. It's that some things most people just don't want. If people
really wanted picturephones, they'd have clamored for them. The
infrastructure has been in place for roll-you-own picturephone (cheap
cameras, networks, appropriate software etc) for years, and no-one bothers
to do this. And it's not just bandwidth---even people with T1s at home, or
computer geeks with ethernet at work just don't bother doing this. The
product just doesn't seem especially wanted---even less so than fun uses
of cameras like coffeecams, weathercams, jennicam etc.

Maynard


