> "Terry C. Shannon" wrote:
> > Note that the API 1GHz demo was done with
> > a hand-selected EV67 (0.25u) bin.
> 
> Pardon my ignorance, but what exactly does this mean ?

When microprocessors are fabbed at a given speed (or bin) there are some
processors that run slower, and some that run faster, than the target
speed. (Many run slower, that's why there's tons of 466MHz and 500MHz
EV6 parts). Samsung/API apparently found a 1GHz chip in one of their
667Mhz or 750MHz EV67 batches, and used this chip for the demo.



