: I booted my VAX just a week ago and today, it wouldn't boot from its
: stock internal drive. After typing boot at the console it pauses for a
: few seconds, never displaying the "-DKA300" message, then returns to a
: console prompt. The drive doesn't spin up. If I type "show dev" it
: appears with the proper identification, but under "numbytes" it says
: "-------". Is it fried or stuck? Or is something else wrong? I hooked up
: an external drive and its size shows up correctly.
: 
: Any tips on removing the thing if it's bad? Or to whack it to get the
: thing spinning? I can't figure out how to work that plastic shelf it's
: on.

The plastic bracket the drive sits in has a blue tab sticking up.  Push it one
way or the other lift the bracket by the strap.

Then, the drive has a metal plate bolted to it.  The plate sits in the plastic
bracket.  On the end of the drive opposite the connectors is a catch, which
holds the drive in place.  Bend it down and push the drive forward until the
metal plate clears the bracket, then lift the drive out.  

        Stu



