cad <cad@truenet.com> writes:
> I've got a problem when i plug my DAT TLZ06 DEC drive on my PC
> I'm using INTRA SERVER 3140U SCSI card
>
> When the PC boots, the menu configuration of the scsi card appears, scans
> the bus and staysin this state.
>
> When the DAT drive is unplugged, no problem at boot and the other drive
> works correctly

  First, make sure the drive is configured appropriately (termination/ID).
Note that the 3140U is an Ultra/Wide controller, so you need to pay par-
ticular attention to termination and cabling - you can only use 2 of the
3 connectors, for example. You may also need to use the 3140U's setup to
change the maximum target negotiation speed to 5MB/sec, either for the
TLZ06 or for all devices.

If that doesn't fix it, take a look at:

http://www.storage.digital.com/homepage/sup_html/techtips/mvtapes/generic.htm

  which explains what jumper to change on a TLZ06 to make it behave as the
industry-standard Connor model it really is.

