X-Accept-Language: en
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Compaq Computer Corporation
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

I think you need to install the Kernel Header and Common Files subset.
That should be OSFBINCOMnnn, where nnn relates to the version of the
OS that you are running (nnn=425 for V4.0D, for example).

Try this:

 /usr/sbin/setld -i | grep OSFBINCOM

If it doesn't say "installed", you will need to install it.

You can get a listing of the contents of that subset using

 /usr/sbin/setld -i OSFBINCOM435

In my case, I've specified 435 for V4.0E, so your actual number
may vary.

-Jeff
