In article <3786BC55.AE37EC6@email.com>, Stephen Eickhoff <operagost@email.com> writes:
>
>Any tips on removing the thing if it's bad? Or to whack it to get the
>thing spinning? I can't figure out how to work that plastic shelf it's
>on.

It does sound as if the disk itself is bad.

Assuming you have successfully removed the top cover of the
VAX4000-60 and are referring to the plastic carrier into
which one or more disks are mounted, look for a small
release lever in one corner of the carrier (it's moulded
as an integral part of the carrier).  Pushing this to
one side (usually 'outwards) will release the latch at the
bottom of the carrier.  It's about 1/2 inch wide.

One some systems, the top of this latch has been broken
off so you have to reach down past the side of the disk
drive to get to it.

