Need to know your hardware a bit better, but the first stage is
to work out how to set the language at the console prompt.
Usually one can just type set language 0 , followed by init to be
presented with a choice at boot time, however on some of the more
obscure/old firmware revisions this may be different(I recall
that the turbo channel 3000's were odd)
After this you need to look at something like dxkeycaps to
configure things in X, although whether or not this works under
CDE I don't know.
If your console is a VT not a keyboard/video head plugged
straight in, then you may need to setup that on it's own, usually
on DEC terminals F3 will get you into setup, although you may
only be able to use this if you first power-cycle the VT then
press F3 when the diagnostic OK message is onscreen.
Then once the VT is set up you need to configure the shell usualy
using the environment variable TERM.

Hope this helps
Adam








