Not specifically, but I built glib-1.2.3 last week on my DU 4.0D (PK3) 
system with no significant problems. I strongly urge you to build with 
DEC C. It's a much better compiler and the resulting code will almost
invariably run faster, often MUCH faster.

NOTE: Always specify the -std option to switch the compiler to ANSI syntax!
I believe I configured it with:
setenv CC cc;setenv CFLAGS "-std -fast";./configure
Of course, this assumes csh or tcsh.
I did Gtk and gimp about the same way.
