> What seems to happen when the tape is loading then the drive all of a sudden
> siezes. 

How much of the tape gets loaded before it seizes ? Does it go far enough into
the loading to be able to actually mount the tape ? Or does it fail before the
tape gets fully mounted ?

Early version of the infamous TK50 had a problem with the plastic leader which
goes in the cartridge to pickup the tape and pull it along the path to the
spool. Failure occured before the tape would be wound into the spool.

I suggest youtake the cover off the TK50 so that you can see the inner spool,
head and other mechanisms, plug the unit back in and carefully watch what
happens as the system attempts to load the tape.



