sense to port the OS to IA-64 (Solaris, like Tru64 UNIX, has
successfully booted on IA-64 emulatorware.)

Of course, the IA-64 port of Solaris renders it feasible for Sun to drop
Sparc should such a move make sense. Sparc has done quite well even
though the architecture is in many cases "behind the pack" in the RISC
performance race. When UltraSparc III starts shipping (early next year?)
methinks it will be at least reasonably competitive with IA-64. And with
EV67 667MHz for that matter.

Terry Shannon



