it did take a little tweaking in my dhcpd.conf file:

group {
	always-reply-rfc1048 on;
	use-host-decl-names on;

	host aragorn {
		hardware ethernet 08:00:2b:39:91:81;
		fixed-address 10.0.0.9;
		option root-path "nb/aragorn/root";
		option host-name "aragorn";
		filename "aragorn/netboot";
	}
}

It was sending out bogus packets before I added the above.  I think the
"always-reply-rfc1048 on" is the key.



