Fergus:
    Your best option is to upgrade to a V4.0x release.  The V3.2x stream you're on
is no longer
    supported.

    If you can't do that,  you have some other less desirable options.   Since
you're barely over
    the limit (8191 vs 8189), try the following in the application you're linking:

        - Reduce the number of GOT entries by declaring, where possible, some of
the globally
           visible procedures and variables "static" as you can.  (assuming your
using C or C++).

        - Remove any unused definitions for global variables or procedures.  Note
the compilers in
           the V4.0x releases will do this for you.

Joe Mario


