:writes:
:> :I'm not sure, but was it not possible to run OpenVMS on a Alphastation XL266?
:>
:>   This is not possible AFAIK.  Definitely not among the supported platforms
:>   for OpenVMS.
..
:    Do you know what's needed that the little XLs don't have?
:    or is it a firmware thing?

  There are no OpenVMS CPU-specific routines available for this box that 
  I am aware of -- each OpenVMS Alpha system has a half-dozen or so images 
  specifically for system support, and each Alpha system requires a new 
  set of these images -- or it must be sufficiently similar to an existing 
  and supported Alpha system to operate via the Dynamic System Recognition 
  (DSR) mechanism. 

  This discussion also presupposes that the hardware has all capabilities 
  necessary for OpenVMS, and I don't know that.  (OpenVMS also requires
  the availability the SRM console for the target system, as well.)

  For some idea of what files are involved for adding support for a "new"
  system, see the Miata kits at the OpenVMS Freeware website.

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
 Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




