Definitely paranoid and hardly aimed at IBM as a number of other
Server vendors sell systems with something called a Systems
Service Processor.

HP actually have gone as far as using the name Hyperplex
for their high end NUMA V-Series AKA Convex. Surely a
direct copy of Sysplex.

The fact that Sun does not call Domains on E10K's Partitions
or PPAR's is a good illustration of the fact that there isn't
some major marketing conspiracy going on.

