> various slimy ... nevermind, I'm not a marketeer. Maybe that's
> why.
>

The acronim SSA is not Sun Storage Architecture but SPARC
Storage Array which was the first FC based Storage Array
from Sun. As it pre-dates IBM-SSA  Sun can hardly be accused
of stealing the name and could be forgiven for thinking that IBM used
SSA just to get at Sun, but that would be paranoid.

Since Sun no longer produces the SPARC Storage Array this can
hardly be a source of contention or much paranoia at IBM.

The problem is more likely a lack of suitable alternative

names for products that havn't allready been used by someone

else.

